      {
        "id": "p14-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $Q_1$, the median and $Q_3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q_1=\\$67\\,000$, median $=\\$81\\,500$, $Q_3=\\$100\\,000$.",
          "worked": "In ascending order, the incomes in thousands of dollars are:\n\n$21,34,34,45,54,54,65,67,67,68,75,78,78,79,81,82,87,89,92,98,98,98,100,102,103,105,112,132,256,345$.\n\nThere are 30 values. The median is the mean of the 15th and 16th values. Each half contains 15 values, so its median is its 8th value.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{81\\,000+82\\,000}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=\\$81\\,500\\\\Q_1&=\\$67\\,000\\\\Q_3&=\\$100\\,000\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the interquartile range.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$33\\,000$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{IQR}&=Q_3-Q_1\\\\\\text{IQR}&=100\\,000-67\\,000\\\\\\text{IQR}&=\\$33\\,000\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Draw a boxplot, showing any outliers.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Outliers: $\\$256\\,000$ and $\\$345\\,000$. Whiskers end at $\\$21\\,000$ and $\\$132\\,000$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1.5\\times\\text{IQR}&=1.5\\times33\\,000\\\\1.5\\times\\text{IQR}&=49\\,500\\\\\\text{Lower boundary}&=67\\,000-49\\,500\\\\\\text{Lower boundary}&=\\$17\\,500\\\\\\text{Upper boundary}&=100\\,000+49\\,500\\\\\\text{Upper boundary}&=\\$149\\,500\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe incomes $\\$256\\,000$ and $\\$345\\,000$ exceed the upper boundary; none is below the lower boundary. Draw the box from $\\$67\\,000$ to $\\$100\\,000$, with median $\\$81\\,500$. The whiskers end at the lowest and highest non-outliers, $\\$21\\,000$ and $\\$132\\,000$; mark both outliers separately.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
